 "redaction_rules": [
  "Lexicon from all /api/v1/agencies entries (parents and sub-agencies): FR 'name' (case-insensitive if multi-word, must start capitalised in text), its natural word order for inverted FR names ('X Department' -> 'Department of X' / 'Department of the X'; same for Office, Bureau, Service, etc.), short_name (split on '/'), slug-derived acronym (initials of slug words minus stop words, >=3 letters).",
  "Printed agency names (raw_name) from the snapshot documents' own agency lists (entries with an API id, or id-less entries shaped like 'Department/Office of ...' or ending in Commission/Board/etc.).",
  "Short names the text defines right after an agency name in parentheses, e.g. '(DOT)', '(the \"Commission\")', are redacted everywhere in that document ('defined_self_name').",
  "Generic self-references (Commission, Board, Bureau, Service, Department, Agency, ...) standing alone, e.g. 'The Commission hereby', 'further Board order', are redacted to [AGENCY] when the noun is a word in the name of one of the document's own listed agencies or a capitalised word in that agency's official description ('Administration' only from names). Not redacted when part of a longer proper name (capitalised word before or after, or followed by 'of/on/for X'). A self-noun right after a full agency name ('... Administration Board') is folded into that [AGENCY]. Parenthetical 'operating as X' names count as defined self-names.",
  "'Secretary of (the) X' where 'Department of X' is an agency name -> 'Secretary of [AGENCY]'.",
  "Exception: an agency short_name/slug acronym is kept in a document whose text defines it, in parentheses, for a phrase that is not an agency name (e.g. 'Emergency Alert System (EAS)'); logged in meta.not_redacted_acronyms. 'USA'/'US' (Army Department short_name) are never redacted.",
  "Exception: a 2-letter short_name preceded by ', ' (address postal code such as 'Washington, DC') is kept.",
  "Verification fix: a frozen alias list (EXTRA_ALIASES) adds official self-names missing from the FR agency list: 'United States Trade Representative' / 'U.S. Trade Representative' / 'Trade Representative' (USTR), 'Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System' / 'Federal Reserve Board' / 'Federal Reserve' (Fed), 'DoN' (Navy), 'Commissioner of Food and Drugs' (FDA); 'Board' is a generic self-noun for the Fed.",
  "Verification fix: an acronym (short_name or slug acronym) of the document's own listed agencies inside a longer code token ('HUDCAPS', 'GSAR', '66VA53') or in another case before a form number ('Ferc-555') is replaced by [AGENCY] ('own_acronym_variant').",
  "All matches replaced by '[AGENCY]'; every replacement logged in meta.redactions."
 ],
 "uncertain": [
  "Interpretation choices (not fixed by the spec): 'short abstract' = under 100 characters; documents with any agency entry lacking an API id are dropped (212 docs, e.g. id-less 'Office of the Secretary'); the 40th-place tie at 11 docs is broken by random.Random(3) (selection_criteria s.5), leaving out the tied labels listed in labels_tied_at_boundary_left_out.",
  "Redaction is lexicon-based (FR agency list plus the frozen alias list), so sub-unit names/acronyms that are not FR agencies stay visible, e.g. NMFS, NEFSC, VHA, BJS, NCSES, OIRA, 'Enforcement Bureau'; statute and program names (Federal Deposit Insurance Act, National Credit Union Share Insurance Fund) and topic words (Veterans, Postal, marine mammals) are content and are kept. 'a Commission Determination' (ITC title formula) is kept because the noun is followed by a capitalised word.",
  "Generic self-reference redaction depends on the document's own agency names/descriptions (i.e. on the label); it removes the cue noun, but whether a noun was redacted is itself weakly label-dependent.",
  "Some short_names used for redaction are also ordinary abbreviations; those defined in the same text for a non-agency phrase are kept (meta.not_redacted_acronyms: EAC, EAS, NSC, FAR in 4 rows); 'USA'/'US' (Army short_name) are never redacted.",
  "Card is long (~36k chars): 40 official FR agency descriptions in full (whitespace normalised).",
  "Many states are generic Paperwork Reduction Act / meeting notices whose agency is hard to infer after redaction; this is kept as sampled (no filtering on difficulty).",
  "FR 'abstract' for 2026-09-24..26 documents may still be revised by the FR after the snapshot; the cached snapshot is the frozen version."
 ],
